# Trivy vulnerability-ignore list for the opensign-server image
# (used via --ignorefile in .github/workflows/opensign-server-rebuild.yml).
#
# WHY THESE ARE ACCEPTED
# The OS layer is NOT ignored: the Dockerfile runs `apt-get dist-upgrade`
# (refreshed every time the base image digest moves -- see
# .opensign-server-base-digest), so the Debian packages + LibreOffice ship at
# their latest point-release and the only fixable CRITICAL/HIGH findings left
# in the image are the Node.js application + npm dependencies below. Every one
# is either baked into the pinned node:22.14.0 image (the npm CLI's own
# transitive tree) or pinned by upstream's apps/OpenSignServer/package-lock.json,
# and each has a newer version on the npm registry that fixes it -- we just
# can't move it without forking OpenSign's dependency tree or floating the
# pinned node:22.14.0 base, both of which this repo deliberately avoids for
# reproducibility.
#
# The 4 fixable CRITICAL findings in this image are tar (CVE-2026-59873, 3
# hits in the npm CLI's bundled tree) and proxy-addr (OpenSign's own express
# dependency). The old lodash / marked / minimist / underscore versions are no
# longer in the image, so their ids were pruned on 2026-10-10.
#
# Lower severities and CVEs with no available fix are reported by Trivy but
# don't block; only fixable CRITICAL/HIGH do (trivy-scan.sh), so a fresh CVE
# in the OS layer or a dependency bump will fail the build until it's either
# patched or explicitly added here with a reason.
#
# Re-check after a node:22.14.0 -> node:X.Y.Z base bump and after each
# OpenSign release: a newer node bundles a newer npm (shrinking the
# node-bundled set) and upstream may have bumped proxy-addr / axios / multer.
# Prune ids Trivy no longer reports (stale entries would silently hide a
# regression back to a vulnerable version).

# --- node:22.14.0's bundled npm (the npm CLI's own dependency tree) --------
# brace-expansion 2.0.1
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# glob 10.4.5
CVE-2025-64756

# ip-address 9.0.5
CVE-2026-69192

# minimatch 9.0.5
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# pacote 19.0.1 + 20.0.0
CVE-2026-9496

# sigstore 3.0.0
CVE-2026-48815

# tar 6.2.1 + 7.4.3
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
CVE-2026-73566

# --- Trivy DB 2026-10-09 refresh: new advisories vs the SAME pinned deps ------
# The tracked OpenSign release did NOT move (still v2.41.3) -- Trivy just
# published advisories against these already-pinned versions. The fix is still
# waiting on an upstream OpenSign dep bump (or a lockfile override, which this
# repo deliberately avoids). All in the apps/OpenSignServer tree. 20 ids; Trivy
# reports 21 findings because the @graphql-tools/utils id hits two installed
# versions (10.8.6 + 9.2.1).
#
# proxy-addr 2.0.7 (CRITICAL; express trust-proxy / IP-spoofing surface)
CVE-2026-90711

# @grpc/grpc-js 1.14.4 (auth bypass via improper peer-cert validation;
# DoSpace/GCP push integrations)
CVE-2026-101916

# axios 1.19.0 (HTTP client: Mailgun / DoSpace / other API calls)
CVE-2026-101898
CVE-2026-101901
CVE-2026-101903
CVE-2026-101905
CVE-2026-101906
CVE-2026-101907
CVE-2026-101909

# multer 2.2.0 (file-upload surface; DoS)
CVE-2026-77037
CVE-2026-77078
CVE-2026-82333

# nodemailer 9.0.5 (SMTP outbound; quadratic-complexity DoS)
GHSA-2x7j-588g-ccc2
GHSA-v53p-9fqp-m79j

# sharp 0.35.3 (image processing; bundled libheif / librsvg)
GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c
GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w

# undici 7.29.0 (HTTP client under gRPC/axios; DoS + cert-validation bypass)
CVE-2026-19534
CVE-2026-84961

# js-yaml 3.15.1 (config parsing; DoS)
CVE-2026-84375

# @graphql-tools/utils 10.8.6 + 9.2.1 (GraphQL layer; DoS via prototype
# pollution in mergeDeep)
CVE-2026-104852
